          "distinct": true,
          "id": "39f28651d1d4741059011da6cbcef2431002c8e9",
          "message": "fix: align govy.Rule WithMessage and WithDetails with general Go API guidelines for printf-like functions (#164)\n\n## Motivation\n\nSee https://github.com/nobl9/govy/issues/140.\n\n## Release Notes\n\nAdded `WithDetailsf` and `WithMessagef` methods to `govy.Rule`, which\nhandle prinf-like formatting. Former `WithDetails` and `WithMessage` now\nonly accept a single string parameter.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n`WithDetails` and `WithMessage` methods of `govy.Rule` now only accept a\nsingle string parameter.\nIn order to use prinf-like functionality, use `WithDetailsf` and\n`WithMessagef`.",
          "timestamp": "2025-10-21T10:01:49+02:00",
          "tree_id": "48116a9a5cd85c1580a0e56ef16d879b4171032e",
          "url": "https://github.com/nobl9/govy/commit/39f28651d1d4741059011da6cbcef2431002c8e9"
