          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8bdc5391cb322b44314da03fd851802ccec1c23d",
          "message": "feat: support index expressions in name inference (#183)\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe property path inference system needed to support index expressions\n(array/slice/map access) to properly handle validation rule names for\ncollection elements. Previously, only direct property access was\nsupported, which limited the ability to infer meaningful property paths\nfor validation rules targeting specific elements in collections.\n\n  ## Summary\n\n  - Added support for index expressions in property path inference:\n- New `findNameInIndexExpr` function to process index expressions and\nappend index notation to property paths\n- New `formatIndexExpr` function to format indices based on their type\n(integer literals, string keys, or variables)\n- Enhanced `getStructFromType` to handle collection types (slices,\narrays, maps) by extracting their element types\n  - Improved JSONPath formatting:\n- Updated `jsonpath.EscapeSegment` to correctly escape single quotes in\nsegments (added `'` to `escapedChars`)\n- String map keys are properly formatted with bracket notation when they\ncontain special characters\n- Added comprehensive test coverage for various scenarios (nested\nindices, slices of pointers, maps with string/integer keys, edge cases)\n- Added debug logging for better diagnostics of unhandled cases in type\nand index expression handling\n- Removed unused `Frame` function and its tests from the `infername`\npackage\n\n  ## Testing\n\nComprehensive unit tests added in `internal/infername/infer_test.go`\ncovering:\n  - Array/slice indexing with integer literals\n- Map access with string keys (simple and with special characters like\ndots)\n  - Nested index expressions (e.g., `matrix[0][1]`)\n  - Slices of pointers\n- Edge cases (function calls in indices, binary expressions, unhandled\ntypes)\n\nJSONPath escaping tests updated in `internal/jsonpath/jsonpath_test.go`\nto verify single quote handling.\n\n  ## Release Notes\n\nAdded support for index expressions in property path inference, enabling\nvalidation rules to properly handle array, slice, and map element access\npatterns like `Students[0].Name` or `Config[\"database.host\"]`.\nJSONPath segment escaping now correctly handles single quotes in\nproperty names.",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-10T15:55:34+01:00",
          "tree_id": "be8bb66c4b5953d3ea052246f820cc3884de3aea",
