          "distinct": true,
          "id": "923afb0f1a93f0ba0b1076c97b500bf960a9069d",
          "message": "feat: JSONPath property paths — Path builder, WithName escaping, PropertyPath rename (#213)\n\n## Motivation\n\nThis PR completes the shift from property names to JSONPath-based\nproperty paths across the public API, CLI, generated metadata, and\nvalidation errors. That is needed to represent nested fields, escaped\nsegments, and map-key selectors without relying on ambiguous dotted\nstrings.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements three tightly coupled pre-v1 issues for proper JSONPath\nhandling:\n\n- **#102** — `WithName` now escapes dots and special characters using\n`jsonpath.EscapeSegment`, producing valid JSONPath bracket notation\n(e.g. `WithName(\"foo.bar\")` → `['foo.bar']`)\n- **#202** — `PropertyError.PropertyName` renamed to `PropertyPath`\n(field + JSON tag `\"propertyPath\"`), along with\n`ExpectedRuleError.PropertyName` in govytest\n- **#212** — New `Path` builder type\n(`govy.NewPath().Name(\"metadata\").Name(\"labels\").Index(0)` →\n`metadata.labels[0]`) and `WithPath` method on `PropertyRules`,\n`PropertyRulesForSlice`, and `PropertyRulesForMap`\n\nAdditional changes:\n- `jsonpath.Join` no longer inserts a dot before bracket-notation\nsegments (`parent['key']` not `parent.['key']`)\n- Inferred field names in the `infername` package are now escaped\n- `Validator.RemovePropertiesByName` escapes input names before\ncomparison\n\nCloses #102\nCloses #202\nCloses #212\n\n## Release Notes\n\ngovy's property identification model was switched from string names to\n[JSONPath](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9535)-based property paths\nacross the API, CLI, generated metadata, and serialized validation\nerrors. It also adds the `jsonpath.Path` builder and `WithPath(...)`\nhelpers while changing escaping and join behavior so dotted or\nspecial-character keys are preserved as single JSONPath segments (see\n`## Breaking Changes` for more details).\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- `govy.PropertyError.PropertyName` was renamed to `PropertyPath`, its\nJSON field changed from `propertyName` to `propertyPath`, and its type\nchanged from `string` to `jsonpath.Path`\n- `govy.NewPropertyError` now accepts a `jsonpath.Path` instead of a\nstring property name\n- `govytest.ExpectedRuleError.PropertyName` was renamed to\n`PropertyPath` and now matches the new serialized field name\n- `govy.Validator.RemovePropertiesByName(...string)` was replaced by\n`RemovePropertiesByPath(...jsonpath.Path)`\n- `InferName*` APIs were renamed to `InferPath*`, including\n`PropertyRules.InferPath`, `Validator.InferPath`, and the exported\n`InferPathMode*` types and constants\n- `pkg/govyconfig` name-inference APIs were renamed to path-inference\nAPIs, including `InferredName` to `InferredPath` and\n`Set/GetInferNameIncludeTestFiles` to `Set/GetInferPathIncludeTestFiles`\n- the `govy infername` CLI subcommand was renamed to `govy inferpath`,\nand generated examples/comments now refer to inferred paths rather than\ninferred names\n- `WithName(\"foo.bar\")` now escapes the input as a single JSONPath\nsegment (`['foo.bar']`) instead of treating dots and special characters\nas raw path text\n- `jsonpath.Join` no longer inserts a dot before bracket-notation\nsegments, so paths now render as `parent['key']` instead of\n`parent.['key']`",
