          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f8c2bc6cd359d0710b4c2e517147592cd0a30abe",
          "message": "feat: add configurable URL validation options (#233)\n\n## Motivation\n\nCurrently URL validation only checks for the most common errors, but\noften times there are other common checks users are forced to implement\nthemselves. I think it would be worthwhile to extend the current\n`rules.URL` signature with opt-in options, which would verify additional\nproperties of the URL.\n\n## Summary\n\nSupport scheme, host, user info, and hostname allow/deny checks in the\nURL rule. Add targeted error messages and tests to cover the new\nvalidation behavior.\n\n## Release Notes\n\nAdded configurable `rules.URL` validation options for enforcing allowed\nschemes, required hosts, disallowed user info, and hostname allow/deny\nlists. URL option failures now use built-in message templates so\napplications can customize or translate them consistently.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-08T18:17:40+02:00",
          "tree_id": "df0a953fa62c0c42c16b02c93b40447ff4ed63ce",
